Objective:

The objective of this project is to develop a Hospital Patient Management System

in C++ using structures, without classes.

Patient details such as ID, name, age, disease and allotted bed number

are stored in a circular doubly linked list,

which allows easy insertion, deletion, searching

and traversal in both forward and backward directions.

Hospital beds are managed using an array

so a free bed can be allotted to each new patient.

Discharged patients are stored in a queue,

which keeps the discharge history

and lets the oldest discharged patient be re-admitted.

The project applies circular linked list, array and queue concepts

to solve a real-world hospital problem efficiently.
